# Integrity lock for the evaluator-owned files of the LOCAL LIVE-MODEL
# SUPERVISOR ACCEPTANCE GATE (spec: /tmp/lv-supervisor-local-acceptance-spec.md,
# sha256 3ed295730058e053a001d831dc5ed937e860d0fca6dae2ae7b3311ac80de337a;
# architecture: /tmp/lv-autonomous-live-content-architecture.md, sha256
# 4704227a99b84089a7fead2ed39b2b605b884edf903d9d65261c930f78071758).
#
# FOURTH EVAL-OWNER FREEZE: re-frozen after a real full live run on a separate
# builder commit exposed two CHECKER defects (no production change could fix
# either).
#
# (1) SAME-PROCESS LOOPBACK + SYNCHRONOUS EXTERNAL CHILD. The evaluator hosts
#     the loopback GitHub double in its own process, yet N4-replay and C-N5
#     launched an external coordinator with execFileSync. The blocked event loop
#     could never answer the child, which connected over TCP and then waited
#     forever at 0% CPU (N4 `coordinator.mjs record-candidate-outcome --reason
#     replay` >3m; C-N5 `coordinator.mjs heal-generator-base` >2m; both had to
#     be terminated). Every external child that can reach the double now runs
#     through the new eval-owned helpers/acceptance-exec.mjs: async, detached
#     into its own process group, bounded by a short per-call timeout, swept by
#     a process-group SIGKILL, and asserted to have COMPLETED or been REJECTED —
#     never merely "did not hang". New eval-owned
#     local-acceptance-deadlock.eval.mjs adds deterministic no-network probes
#     DL1-DL5, including a discriminating negative control that reproduces the
#     defect under its own bound, and a static scan (DL4) that fails if any
#     frozen path reintroduces a synchronous child carrying the double.
#
# (2) LEXICAL CROSS-PROCESS PATH CONTAINMENT. N3-shape compared a child's
#     `process.cwd()` against a lexically built `<state>/work` prefix; on macOS
#     the child reports `/private/var/...` for the evaluator's `/var/...`
#     directory, so a lint invocation that provably occurred was reported as
#     none. Both sides are now canonicalized (fs.realpathSync.native) before
#     comparison, and containment is TIGHTENED to a real path-segment boundary.
#     The exact repoRoot-script and relative data-path assertions are unchanged.
#     New deterministic probes PC1-PC3 (in local-acceptance-probes.eval.mjs)
#     reproduce the divergence with a symlinked parent on any POSIX platform and
#     fail if lexical containment, or a loosened one, returns.
#
# Also: N4 now rejects an absent/null runRow.topic_key at the preceding required
# boundary (N4-topic-key) and refuses to pass a literal null into the
# coordinator, so a missing early topic persistence fails promptly by name.
#
# The file set grew by helpers/acceptance-exec.mjs and
# local-acceptance-deadlock.eval.mjs (13 -> 15). Every file below is eval-owned
# and FROZEN.
#
# These files are FROZEN. The implementation builder must not edit, weaken,
# delete, re-scope, or restage any of them. Maker != checker: any change to an
# eval-owned path is a spec/eval-owner change and an automatic FAIL of the
# acceptance review until the eval owner re-freezes.
#
# Verify (from the repository root; every line must print OK and exit 0):
#
#   shasum -a 256 -c evals/local-supervisor-acceptance.sha256
#
